<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n25278" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διαμιλλ-άομαι</span></b> , fut.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ησομαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Str.
					17.1.11
				</span></i>
			:—<i>contend hotly, strive earnestly,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δέκα πρὸς δέκα ἀλλήλοις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Lg.</u>
					833e
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινί</span>
			<i>with</i> one, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>R.</u>
				516e
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρός τινα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					16.21.6
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. περί τινος</span> about a
			thing, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				517d
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινὶ ἐν λόγοις καὶ ἐν
			ἔργοις</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				563a
			</span></i>: c. gen. rei, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. λειοτέρας ὁδοῦ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Lg.</u>
					833b
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινὶ περὶ δεῖπνα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Them.</u>
					5
				</span></i>
			: pf.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διημίλληται</span> in pass. sense, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Par.</u>
				58
			</span></i>.</div>
